  "body": "See discussion at https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7782\r\n\r\nCurrently the browser behavior around range responses are as follows:\r\n- WebKit is very strict, requiring servers to serve the content range requested and ignores `200` responses\r\n- Chromium allows `200` responses and mismatches\r\n- From my understanding, Gecko ignores the Content-Range response header, and assumes the response complies, taking its data.\r\n\r\nThe aforementioned PR makes the spec somewhat aligned with the \"ground truth\" of Gecko & Chromium, however per the discussion on the PR it's far from a consensus, as this requires user-agents to manage buffering of long media resources (see https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7782#issuecomment-1092640249). \r\n\r\nI personally think there is merit in WebKit's position and wanted to keep the discussion live due to lack of consensus.",
